uld find that  uh that  b is not pulled down and b is not  present in the pull down fraction so in  order to detect whether b is present in  the pull down fraction or b is not  present in the pull up down fraction we  would proceed by these steps  so what we would do we would collect  this pull-down fraction and we would  process this pull-down fraction and load  it on a sds-page gel a protein gel and  we would run the protein gel  so after running the protein gel  what we would do we would perform a  wasting blot  and in this western blot we would give  the antibody against protein b  so basically  we pulled down a and now we are  performing the western blot  using the antibody against b  and  if in the western blot if in in the  western blot the diagram of the western  blot we can show that that uh in the  pull down fraction  uh b is present  then we can say  a and b are interacting so we have  pulled down a here and we have loaded  the pull down fraction here and we  expect that in the pull down fraction b  is present so b would be present in this  particular jail and  b would be blotted  in the pvdf membrane so when we put  antibody against b we can see band  against b so b  these bands here so these are the  loading controls like beta acting band  so these  bands  represent b over here  so from this particular  western blot uh profile we can say that  our protein p is actually present in  this pull down fraction so that is how  we can get an idea that whether two  proteins are interacting inside a cell  or not  so there could be two possibilities  either they are interacting they are not  interacting so let's say we have a  control acting band beta acting brand  and this bit acting band is a loading  control so it would be present in the  either conditions whether b is present  or whether b is not present so if b is  present we would get a positive band for  b when we are blotting  the gel  after running the pull down fraction  when we are blotting gel we would get a  positive band for b  and  if b is not present in the pull-down  fraction that means if we think that b  is not actually interacting with a then  what would happen there would be no band  for b but there would be  the loading control the  control band would be there the loading  control band would be there but there  would be no band for b so from this from  this particular graph we can say that  these  two proteins a and b are not interacting  most likely they are not interacting but  from this graph we can say that protein  a and protein b are interacting because  we have first pulled down a with a  particularly monoclonal antibody coated  bit and then in that pulldown fraction  we are able to show that b is present so  we can say that inside the cell in vivo  situation a and b are interacting  together that is why we are seeing the  band in the b  i hope you enjoyed this video  and this video is useful to you and if  you like my video please give it a quick  thumbs up and thank you and don't forget  to subscribe
 

